<p>
    <strong>Core Gameplan:</strong> A lot like Landstill: Psychatog tries to
    control the early game while building toward an <a
        href="#"
        class="card-hover"
        data-card-name="Upheaval">Upheaval</a
    > plus <a
        href="#"
        class="card-hover"
        data-card-name="Psychatog">Psychatog</a
    > finish. The problem for them is that Replenish has so many threats (<a
        href="#"
        class="card-hover"
        data-card-name="Opalescence">Opalescence</a
    >, <a
        href="#"
        class="card-hover"
        data-card-name="Parallax Wave">Parallax Wave</a
    >, <a href="#" class="card-hover" data-card-name="Replenish"
        >Replenish</a
    >) that you run their counters and removal dry before they hit the mana
    to go off.
</p>
<p>
    <strong>Sideboard Strategy:</strong> Turn into a control deck. Bring in
    taxing effects like <a
        href="#"
        class="card-hover"
        data-card-name="Defense Grid">Defense Grid</a
    > and <a
        href="#"
        class="card-hover"
        data-card-name="Meddling Mage">Meddling Mage</a
    > along with instant-speed disruption (<a
        href="#"
        class="card-hover"
        data-card-name="Abeyance">Abeyance</a
    >, <a
        href="#"
        class="card-hover"
        data-card-name="Arcane Denial">Arcane Denial</a
    >). Psychatog loads up on anti-enchantment cards and card-draw hate after
    board, so switching to <a
        href="#"
        class="card-hover"
        data-card-name="Exalted Angel">Exalted Angel</a
    > gives you a fast clock that dodges all of it.
</p>
